#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192617 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3da4448-71cc-5671-8f32-a9f293ad5054" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "61c51284-18f0-5398-857b-7687228e8df8" :question/math-academy-id "e-7985" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{x^2}{9}, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{36}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192618 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8322a1ba-7608-53de-88d9-e360ca8025cd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "c755eddf-3b0d-5a33-aa13-e6a3f7da4244" :question/math-academy-id "e-7986" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[7X-4].$\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{3x^2}{7}, \\quad 1 <        x <        2\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[7X-4] = 7 \\textrm E[X] - 4\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{28}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{28}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[7X-4] & =7\\text{E}[X]-4 \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{45}{28}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192619 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b84b8fb-5ad7-5c4f-af44-b6d1dc9310c1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable With a Piecewise PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "3a11b9e3-60c8-57f3-8ec6-4ff378d0db62" :question/math-academy-id "e-7987" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n![](images/98/98b997e3016e9ca5538863c3faa19ac017f90e8bcdeba40e09c03aba28c4ace4.svg)" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{3x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}|}_{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8})|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{31}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3da4448-71cc-5671-8f32-a9f293ad5054" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26751660-b10c-52b5-b32b-8fb5a1bdd82c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424057} {:answer/id #uuid "90ca78b7-c93c-5e6a-8cc5-7647d2cc2740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424068} {:answer/id #uuid "91379b67-0509-5582-a25b-36b84489e757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424069} {:answer/id #uuid "c385dfd9-ebdb-5db3-ac8a-7fa4bb79f925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424075} {:answer/id #uuid "cb89e563-276d-50d6-a32f-f52c04c6441b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90ca78b7-c93c-5e6a-8cc5-7647d2cc2740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424068} :answer-field/id #uuid "5eb8932f-143b-578f-a0db-bb4cc2c246c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424081}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7821024d-c004-5d99-9790-91a65c2602fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-130751" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=6x(1-x),\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot 6x(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(2{x}^{3}-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{2})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b84b8fb-5ad7-5c4f-af44-b6d1dc9310c1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable With a Piecewise PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e7252d1-7bec-51e8-895b-5c303264ccf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424055} {:answer/id #uuid "13c231a4-02c9-519e-a16e-fac887b7ebc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424056} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf10b9f-0537-5d79-9473-d19b73e91528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424071} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e07a66-e2fe-5302-a36e-006523c84d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424072} {:answer/id #uuid "b60edc09-3248-59be-ad60-c9699fb3762c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b60edc09-3248-59be-ad60-c9699fb3762c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424073} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee00c64-0bcc-5caf-9fda-20fec973369a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0312f13e-9d46-503a-8af4-69a3bd5d2f16" :question/math-academy-id "q-130870" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{x}, & -\\sqrt{e}<x<-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & -1\\le x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x{|}_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}+{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{e}+\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{e}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b84b8fb-5ad7-5c4f-af44-b6d1dc9310c1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable With a Piecewise PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33e3d064-30ad-5eab-99b7-4055df83c43b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424059} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab28cb4-c411-518a-b8f9-3b843cb43bb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e-1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424066} {:answer/id #uuid "828c703f-f7c1-5221-a107-3b628a52c6ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e+1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424067} {:answer/id #uuid "c327ff22-8621-594a-a52d-99bb4e2941b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424074} {:answer/id #uuid "de4f8756-22a2-5a93-8cf4-1f6ce720de08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c327ff22-8621-594a-a52d-99bb4e2941b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424074} :answer-field/id #uuid "c45ae753-611c-5337-a1ef-57b485b3183d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "713f9e9d-4bae-5fb8-b6da-37cc8d4aaf0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130872" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x}{5}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5x}, & 1\\le x<e\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{6x}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{5}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{2x}{5}|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{2e}{5}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424086 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3da4448-71cc-5671-8f32-a9f293ad5054" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30c9587e-71e5-566c-a7c0-2ca7d8543d06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424058} {:answer/id #uuid "44d46d21-8790-5b62-b822-b15cfffb758c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424060} {:answer/id #uuid "6ddc91ad-5eb5-580c-aec8-05f1a65ef396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424063} {:answer/id #uuid "77b11337-68cc-5792-80b0-2420a4a46582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424065} {:answer/id #uuid "f27e69cb-8e5b-5f27-b7bd-fd886daab64b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77b11337-68cc-5792-80b0-2420a4a46582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424065} :answer-field/id #uuid "174c2ec8-e1f1-51fa-bb13-18381c6477ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3754a443-839d-5055-afd8-172b5271b8be" :question/math-academy-id "q-90386" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{1}{3},\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{36}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193400 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8322a1ba-7608-53de-88d9-e360ca8025cd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "beb8e572-d355-5b9e-9db7-fad6bf9cc428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192328} {:answer/id #uuid "f5523beb-c1ce-57b7-95d3-67749a5266b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192329} {:answer/id #uuid "2e80ca0c-6a04-5c09-9c17-2034f81e97e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192330} {:answer/id #uuid "437fe653-fd9f-53eb-9e04-17a88b8d4bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192331} {:answer/id #uuid "4e170e19-e1b1-5e95-b461-a4cb6c8f7ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "beb8e572-d355-5b9e-9db7-fad6bf9cc428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192328} :answer-field/id #uuid "b941308d-d487-55e0-9a91-cc64a7bfa6a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6fdbb6b-bf50-55db-8f1b-9ba9143d4ac9" :question/math-academy-id "q-90393" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[3X-4].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{1}{4},\\,2<x<6\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[3X-4]=3\\text{E}[X]-4\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{24}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8})|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}-(-\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[3X-4] & =3\\text{E}[X]-4 \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{14}{3}-4 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8322a1ba-7608-53de-88d9-e360ca8025cd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "493212b2-48a2-5243-a9c9-38c8ad4f746e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424061} {:answer/id #uuid "58440bd6-5f91-58ba-8252-d7a100bf2bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424062} {:answer/id #uuid "73b5e0f3-2a9f-5fb2-98c7-0b0e8e8b99a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424064} {:answer/id #uuid "955a942b-f31a-5981-97c6-1e16d11283d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424070} {:answer/id #uuid "fd63a7fa-8fda-54c4-8de2-4fa95151be2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "493212b2-48a2-5243-a9c9-38c8ad4f746e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424061} :answer-field/id #uuid "807b5737-467e-51a3-be92-0cedb472eebd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6256bcf-ce6c-599c-ab9b-d80ffcce67e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-90455" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[8X-3].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9},\\,0<x<3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[8X-3]=8\\text{E}[X]-3\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{36}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[8X-3] & =8\\text{E}[X]-3 \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{9}{4}-3 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
